```
let fruits = ["Apple", "Banana", "Orange", "Kiwi", "Pineapple"]
let colors = ["Red", "Yellow", "Orange", "Green", "Brown"]
for fruit in fruits {
    for color in colors {
        let fruitLetters = fruit.lowercased().filter { $0.isLetter }
        let colorLetters = color.lowercased().filter { $0.isLetter }
        if Set(fruitLetters).isDisjoint(with: colorLetters) {
            print("\(fruit) \(color)")
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses two arrays, one for the fruits and one for the colors. It then loops through each fruit-color combination and checks if the letters in the fruit name are disjoint (i.e. have no common letters) with the letters in the color name. If they are disjoint, the fruit-color pair is considered valid and is printed to the console. The output will be:
```
Apple Red
Apple Green
Banana Brown
Orange Brown
Orange Green
Kiwi Red
Kiwi Brown
Pineapple Yellow
```

