            padding: 20px 30px;
            background-color: white;
            position: relative;
            border-radius: 6px;
        }
        @media screen and (max-width: 600px) {
            .timeline::after {
                left: 31px;
            }
            .container {
                width: 100%;
                padding-left: 70px;
                padding-right: 25px;
            }
            .container::after {
                left: 15px;
            }
            .left::after, .right::after {
                right: auto;
                left: 15px;
                border-color: transparent white transparent transparent;
            }
            .left {
                left: 0;
            }
            .right {
                left: 0;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Textile Machinery during the Industrial Revolution</h1>
    <div class="timeline">
        <div class="container left">
            <div class="content">
                <h2>Spinning Jenny</h2>
                <img src="spinning_jenny.jpg" alt="Spinning Jenny">
                <p>The Spinning Jenny was invented by James Hargreaves in 1764. It allowed one person to spin multiple threads at once, increasing productivity and reducing the cost of production. This led to an increase in the demand for textiles and the growth of the textile industry. However, it also led to a decrease in the demand for skilled labor and the exploitation of child labor.</p>
            </div>
