        <div class="container right">
            <div class="content">
                <h2>Water Frame</h2>
                <img src="water_frame.jpg" alt="Water Frame">
                <p>The Water Frame was invented by Richard Arkwright in 1769. It used water power to spin multiple threads at once, further increasing productivity and reducing the cost of production. This led to the growth of the factory system and the concentration of labor in urban areas. It also led to poor working conditions and the exploitation of women and children.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="container left">
            <div class="content">
                <h2>Power Loom</h2>
                <img src="power_loom.jpg" alt="Power Loom">
                <p>The Power Loom was invented by Edmund Cartwright in 1784. It used water power to automate the weaving process, further increasing productivity and reducing the cost of production. This led to the growth of the textile industry and the development of new markets for textiles. However, it also led to the displacement of skilled weavers and the exploitation of women and children in the factories.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <script>
        var timeline = document.querySelector('.timeline');
        var containers = document.querySelectorAll('.container');
        var bodyRect = document.body.getBoundingClientRect();
        var firstContainer = containers[0].getBoundingClientRect().top - bodyRect.top;
        window.addEventListener('scroll', function() {
            if (window.pageYOffset >= firstContainer) {
                timeline.classList.add('sticky');
            } else {
                timeline.classList.remove('sticky');
            }
            containers.forEach(function(container) {
                var containerRect = container.getBoundingClientRect();
                var containerTop = containerRect.top - bodyRect.top;
                var containerBottom = containerRect.bottom - bodyRect.top;
                if (containerTop <= window.innerHeight * 0.6 && containerBottom >= window.innerHeight * 0.4) {
                    container.classList.add('active');
                } else {
                    container.classList.remove('active');
                }
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```
This code creates a timeline with three containers, each containing the description and image of a machine. The timeline is sticky and becomes fixed to the top of the page when it is scrolled past. When a container is in the center of the viewport, it becomes active and its content is highlighted. You can modify the content of the containers and add more containers to create a more comprehensive timeline of textile machinery during the Industrial Revolution.

