2. Implement the modified selection sort algorithm:
The selection sort algorithm works by repeatedly finding the minimum (or maximum) element from the unsorted part of the array and putting it at the beginning (or end) of the sorted part. To sort in descending order, we'll find the maximum element instead of the minimum. Here's how you can implement it using a loop:
```
void selectionSortDesc(MyClass arr[], int n) {
  for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
    int max_idx = i;
    for (int j = i + 1; j < n; j++) {
      if (arr[j].value > arr[max_idx].value) {
        max_idx = j;
      }
    }
    if (max_idx != i) {
      MyClass temp = arr[i];
      arr[i] = arr[max_idx];
      arr[max_idx] = temp;
    }
  }
}
```
