To create a linked list data structure in PHP using a SQL database, you can create a table with columns for the node ID, data, and a reference to the next node in the list. Here is an example schema for the table:
```
CREATE TABLE linked_list (
    id INT(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
    data VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
    next_id INT(11) DEFAULT NULL,
    PRIMARY KEY (id),
    FOREIGN KEY (next_id) REFERENCES linked_list(id)
);
```
To add a node to the list, you can insert a new row into the table with the data for the node and the ID of the next node in the list. If the node is the last one in the list, the next_id column should be set to NULL. Here is an example function that adds a node to the list:
```
function addNode($data, $next_id) {
    $conn = new mysqli("localhost", "username", "password", "database");
    $stmt = $conn->prepare("INSERT INTO linked_list (data, next_id) VALUES (?, ?)");
    $stmt->bind_param("si", $data, $next_id);
    $stmt->execute();
    $stmt->close();
    $conn->close();
}
```
To remove a node from the list, you can update the next_id column of the previous node to point to the next node in the list, and then delete the row for the node you want to remove. Here is an example function that removes a node from the list:
```
function removeNode($id) {
    $conn = new mysqli("localhost", "username", "password", "database");
    $stmt = $conn->prepare("SELECT next_id FROM linked_list WHERE id = ?");
    $stmt->bind_param("i", $id);
    $stmt->execute();
    $stmt->bind_result($next_id);
    $stmt->fetch();
    $stmt->close();
    $stmt = $conn->prepare("UPDATE linked_list SET next_id = ? WHERE next_id = ?");
    $stmt->bind_param("ii", $next_id, $id);
    $stmt->execute();
    $stmt->close();
    $stmt = $conn->prepare("DELETE FROM linked_list WHERE id = ?");
    $stmt->bind_param("i", $id);
    $stmt->execute();
    $stmt->close();
    $conn->close();
}
```
To traverse the list and retrieve data from specific nodes using SQL queries, you can use a SELECT statement with a JOIN to follow the next_id references in the table. Here is an example function that retrieves the data for all nodes in the list:
```
function getAllNodes() {
    $conn = new mysqli("localhost", "username", "password", "database");
    $sql = "SELECT l1.id, l1.data, l2.id AS next_id FROM linked_list l1 LEFT JOIN linked_list l2 ON l1.next_id = l2.id";
