public class VaRModel {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
    double portfolioValue = scanner.nextDouble();
    double confidenceLevel = scanner.nextDouble();
    double volatility = scanner.nextDouble();
    double timeHorizon = scanner.nextDouble();

    double zScore = getZScore(confidenceLevel);
    double VaR = portfolioValue * zScore * volatility * Math.sqrt(timeHorizon);

    System.out.println("VaR: " + VaR);
  }

  private static double getZScore(double confidenceLevel) {
    switch((int) (confidenceLevel * 100)) {
      case 90:
        return 1.645;
      case 95:
        return 1.96;
      case 99:
        return 2.33;
      default:
        return 0;
    }
  }
}
```
This code takes in the portfolio value, confidence level, volatility, and time horizon as inputs and calculates the VaR using the z-score method.
